    "title": "Drunk driver leaves path of destruction southeast of downtown - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Gracie Sherrow ,\n1 hours ago FORT WAYNE, Ind. (WANE) - Fort Wayne Police are investigating a crash southeast of downtown Fort Wayne that was caused by a drunk driver.\nPolice responded to the 1600 block of Lewis Street in response to reports of a crash on Wednesday evening.\nFWPD told WANE 15 personnel on scene that they believe a drunk driver in a pickup truck ran over a tree, hit a parked car, and then lost the lawn mower and bicycle in the truck bed along the road.\nA tree on Lewis Street now horizontal after a drunk driver crashed their truck. A parked car and lawnmower lie on Lewis Street after a drunk driver blew through. Drunk driver leaves path of destruction southeast of downtown. The driver traveled about three blocks to the west before coming to a stop near the intersection of Lewis Street and South Anthony Boulevard. Police did not provide the condition of the driver.\nPolice have temporarily blocked off Lewis Street from Winter Street to Anthony Boulevard as they work to gather evidence and clear the scene of the crash.\nNo other persons were involved or injured in the crash.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed.\nFor the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WANE 15.",
    "summary": "Police responded to the 1600 block of Lewis Street in response to reports of a crash on Wednesday evening. FWPD told WANE 15 personnel on scene that they believe a drunk driver in a pickup truck ran over a tree, hit a parked car, and then lost the lawn mower and bicycle in the truck bed along the road. A parked car and lawnmower lie on Lewis Street after a drunk driver blew through. The driver traveled about three blocks to the west before coming to a stop near the intersection of Lewis Street and South Anthony Boulevard.",
